  "analyst_version": "0.1.0",

  "_comment": "Config for Mode B (Legacy Business Rearchitecture) only. Separate file from thresholds.json (Mode A) deliberately - the two modes reason about different evidence and must not share thresholds by accident. Every keyword list is a GENERIC REASONING CATEGORY, not a specific industry or company - see README's Mode B section for why (task requirement: do not hard-code industries or outcomes).",

  "_comment_constraint_taxonomy": "Each bucket names the SHAPE of a historical constraint, generalized from the task's own examples (warehouse inventory, intermediaries, branch networks, manual coordination, vertical integration, safety buffers) without hard-coding those industries. `legacy_markers` describe the WORKAROUND/STRUCTURE a business built because of the constraint (usually present in current_carrier/process). `reason_markers` are words that, when they appear NEAR a legacy_marker, suggest the text itself is stating WHY the structure exists (pushes evidence from INFERRED toward OBSERVED).",
  "constraint_taxonomy": {
    "buffer_inventory": {
      "legacy_markers": ["warehouse", "inventory", "stockpile", "backlog", "excess capacity", "safety stock", "battery storage", "storage capacity", "curtailment"],
