  "_comment_evidence_markers": "Two DIRECTIONS of change language. A text can mention the old constraint (e.g. 'batteries aren't free') while explicitly arguing it is STILL BINDING - that must not be read as weakening. Only explicit weakening/change language, ideally co-located with an enabler_taxonomy hit, counts as evidence the constraint has weakened.",
  "still_binding_markers": ["aren't free", "isn't free", "not free", "still requires", "still needs", "still require",
